{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>that your ox and your donkey may rest</b> — since the word \"לְמַעַן\" (in order that) is like \"בַּעֲבוּר\" (for the sake of), the verse means to say: six days you shall do all your work, in the house and in the field, for the sake of rest on the seventh — the son of your maidservant and the stranger — all of them being witnesses to the act of Creation, in the same sense as \"what you bake, bake\" (Exodus 16:23). And so it says (Exodus 20:9), \"Six days you shall labor and do all your work,\" as I explained there."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:14:36.723083421Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}